  "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}+{30}^{∘} & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2}+{30}^{∘} & ={300}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & ={60}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2} & ={300}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & ={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & \\frac{x}{2} & ={270}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {720}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={540}^{∘}+n\\cdot {720}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<{180}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-{660}^{∘}$ and $x=-{180}^{∘}.$  We reject the solution $-{660}^{∘}$ since it lies outside the domain of interest.\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={60}^{∘}$ and $x={540}^{∘}.$  We reject the solution ${540}^{∘}$ since it lies outside the domain of interest.\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-{180}^{∘}\\le x<{180}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={-180}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={60}^{∘}.\n$$",
